      {
        "id": "def-td-thermodynamic-limit-contract",
        "kind": "definition",
        "domain": "physics",
        "title": "Finite-state thermodynamic-limit contract",
        "reference": "items/def-td-thermodynamic-limit-contract.md",
        "design_state": "Step 1 complete draft; readiness recorded separately.",
        "dependency_level": 3,
        "deps": [
          "def-td-equilibrium-state-domain",
          "def-td-si-quantities",
          "def-natural-numbers",
          "def-tdmath-countable-canonical-model"
        ],
        "justified_by": [],
        "forward_refs": [],
        "dependency_roles": {
          "def-td-equilibrium-state-domain": "formulation-prerequisite",
          "def-td-si-quantities": "formulation-prerequisite",
          "def-natural-numbers": "mathematical-premise",
          "def-tdmath-countable-canonical-model": "mathematical-premise"
        },
        "physical_scope": "A specified sequence of finite-state macroscopic models at positive temperature with a declared density, interactions, boundary conditions, and normalization; no limiting existence, ensemble equivalence, or critical singularity is asserted.",
        "inventory_expansion_required": false,
        "statement": "A **finite-state thermodynamic-limit contract** specifies a sequence $(X_k,E_k,g_k,V_k,n_k)_{k\\in\\mathbb N}$, where $\\mathbb N$ is the positive-integer index set of [[def-natural-numbers]], each $X_k$ is a finite nonempty state set, $E_k:X_k\\to\\mathbb R$ assigns finite energies in joules, $g_k:X_k\\to(0,\\infty)$ assigns positive dimensionless weights, $V_k>0$ is physical volume in $\\mathrm{m^3}$, and, for one declared species, $n_k>0$ is its amount in moles. A fixed-density sequence has $V_k\\to\\infty$ and $n_k/V_k\\to\\rho\\in(0,\\infty)$ in $\\mathrm{mol\\,m^{-3}}$. Boundary conditions, interaction rules, and the choice of a volume or amount normalization are part of the contract and must be held fixed or explicitly tracked as $k$ varies.",
        "provenance": {
          "statement": "ai-altered",
          "proof": "not-applicable"
        },
        "sources": {
          "references": [
            {
              "title": "David Tong, Statistical Physics, author-hosted complete lecture notes, Chapter 5, §5.4.3",
              "url": "https://davidtong.org/teaching/statistical-physics/statmechhtml/S5"
            },
            {
              "title": "Konstantin K. Likharev, Essential Graduate Physics: Statistical Mechanics, §§4.1–4.2",
              "url": "https://phys.libretexts.org/Bookshelves/Thermodynamics_and_Statistical_Mechanics/Essential_Graduate_Physics_-_Statistical_Mechanics_%28Likharev%29/04%3A_Phase_Transitions/4.01%3A_First_order_phase_transitions"
            }
          ]
        },
        "library": "physics"
      },
      {
        "id": "pthm-td-fixed-tp-reaction-potential-minimum",
        "kind": "physics-theorem",
        "domain": "physics",
        "title": "Fixed-temperature and fixed-pressure potential minimum with internal reactions",
        "reference": "items/pthm-td-fixed-tp-reaction-potential-minimum.md",
        "design_state": "Step 1 complete draft; readiness recorded separately.",
        "dependency_level": 7,
        "deps": [
          "def-td-equilibrium-state-domain",
          "def-td-si-quantities",
          "def-td-isolated-compound-feasible-set",
          "post-td-bulk-additivity",
          "post-td-concave-fundamental-entropy",
          "post-td-first-law-energy",
          "post-td-macroscopic-second-law",
          "post-td-entropy-maximum"
        ],
        "justified_by": [],
        "forward_refs": [],
        "dependency_roles": {
          "def-td-equilibrium-state-domain": "formulation-prerequisite",
          "def-td-si-quantities": "formulation-prerequisite",
          "def-td-isolated-compound-feasible-set": "formulation-prerequisite",
          "post-td-bulk-additivity": "physical-assumption",
          "post-td-concave-fundamental-entropy": "physical-assumption",
          "post-td-first-law-energy": "physical-assumption",
          "post-td-macroscopic-second-law": "physical-assumption",
          "post-td-entropy-maximum": "physical-assumption"
        },
        "physical_scope": "A closed reacting system at fixed positive reservoir temperature and fixed external pressure, with internal stoichiometric changes and the exact ideal-reservoir/store model stated here; no external matter exchange, omitted work channel, nonideal reservoir, or kinetic relaxation claim is included.",
        "inventory_expansion_required": true,
        "statement": "Fix a system at a positive temperature $T_0$ and external pressure $p_0>0$. Internal reaction extents may vary in a declared feasible set, but no species crosses the system's outer boundary. The system contacts only an ideal thermal reservoir at $T_0$ and an ideal pressure store at $p_0$; all other work coordinates and excluded-energy changes are absent. Let $U$ be system internal energy in joules, $V$ volume in $\\mathrm{m^3}$, and $S$ system entropy in $\\mathrm{J\\,K^{-1}}$. Define the constrained potential\n\\[\n\\Phi_{T_0,p_0}:=U+p_0V-T_0S.\n\\]\nFor every admitted spontaneous endpoint change, $\\Delta\\Phi_{T_0,p_0}\\le0$. If the system-plus-reservoir-plus-store endpoint is an attained global entropy maximum on its exact feasible set, then the corresponding system endpoint attains a global minimum of $\\Phi_{T_0,p_0}$ over the induced feasible reaction states. This is a conditional model deduction; it does not assert that arbitrary fixed-$T,p$ reactions have this preparation or that the system reaches the minimum dynamically.",
        "provenance": {
          "statement": "ai-altered",
          "proof": "ai-altered"
        },
        "sources": {
          "references": [
            {
              "title": "David Tong, Statistical Physics, author-hosted complete lecture notes, §§4.3–4.4",
              "url": "https://davidtong.org/teaching/statistical-physics/statmechhtml/S4"
            }
          ]
        },
        "library": "physics",
        "strategy": "direct"
      },
      {
