      {
        "id": "pthm-td-reaction-boundary-equilibrium",
        "kind": "physics-theorem",
        "domain": "physics",
        "title": "Reaction equilibrium conditions at interior and boundary amounts",
        "reference": "items/pthm-td-reaction-boundary-equilibrium.md",
        "design_state": "Step 1 complete draft; readiness recorded separately.",
        "dependency_level": 9,
        "deps": [
          "def-td-phase-and-coexistence-domain",
          "def-td-si-quantities",
          "def-td-temperature-pressure-chemical-potential",
          "def-td-legendre-potentials",
          "pthm-td-fixed-tp-reaction-potential-minimum",
          "pthm-td-potential-differentials",
          "lem-tdmath-stoichiometric-tangent-cone",
          "def-td-equilibrium-state-domain"
        ],
        "justified_by": [],
        "forward_refs": [],
        "dependency_roles": {
          "def-td-phase-and-coexistence-domain": "formulation-prerequisite",
          "def-td-si-quantities": "formulation-prerequisite",
          "def-td-temperature-pressure-chemical-potential": "formulation-prerequisite",
          "def-td-legendre-potentials": "formulation-prerequisite",
          "pthm-td-fixed-tp-reaction-potential-minimum": "physical-result",
          "pthm-td-potential-differentials": "physical-result",
          "lem-tdmath-stoichiometric-tangent-cone": "mathematical-premise",
          "def-td-equilibrium-state-domain": "formulation-prerequisite"
        },
        "physical_scope": "Local C1 constrained Gibbs-potential charts for a declared internal reaction network at fixed positive reservoir temperature and pressure; boundary conclusions require the explicit C1 extension to zero amounts stated here.",
        "inventory_expansion_required": false,
        "statement": "Fix $C\\ge1$ species and $R\\ge1$ declared internal reaction extents. Let $\\nu\\in\\mathbb R^{C\\times R}$ be the dimensionless stoichiometric matrix, let $n^0\\in[0,\\infty)^C$ have units mol, and let $\\xi\\in\\mathbb R^R$ have units mol. The amount vector is $n(\\xi)=n^0+\\nu\\xi$, and the nonnegative-amount feasible extent set is\n\\[\n\\mathcal F_\\nu:=\\{\\xi\\in\\mathbb R^R:n^0+\\nu\\xi\\in[0,\\infty)^C\\}.\n\\]\nFix $T_0>0$ and $p_0$ in a declared natural-variable chart. Let $\\Phi(\\xi)$ be the constrained Gibbs potential on an open neighborhood $U$ of an equilibrium extent $\\xi_*$, and assume the model supplies a finite $C^1$ extension through every zero-amount boundary point under consideration. On $U$, assume\n\\[\nD\\Phi(\\xi)[h]=\\sum_{j=1}^C\\mu_j(\\xi)(\\nu h)_j=(\\nu^{\\mathsf T}\\mu(\\xi))\\cdot h,\n\\]\nwhere $\\mu_j$ are the molar chemical potentials in $\\mathrm{J\\,mol^{-1}}$. This extension and derivative identity are not supplied by the positive-mole phase chart itself.",
        "provenance": {
          "statement": "ai-altered",
          "proof": "ai-altered"
        },
        "sources": {
          "references": [
            {
              "title": "David Tong, Statistical Physics, author-hosted complete lecture notes, §4.4",
              "url": "https://davidtong.org/teaching/statistical-physics/statmechhtml/S4"
            },
            {
              "title": "Konstantin K. Likharev, Essential Graduate Physics: Statistical Mechanics, §4.1 First-order phase transitions",
              "url": "https://phys.libretexts.org/Bookshelves/Thermodynamics_and_Statistical_Mechanics/Essential_Graduate_Physics_-_Statistical_Mechanics_%28Likharev%29/04%3A_Phase_Transitions/4.01%3A_First_order_phase_transitions"
            }
          ]
        },
        "library": "physics",
        "strategy": "direct"
      },
      {
        "id": "pthm-td-clapeyron-local",
        "kind": "physics-theorem",
        "domain": "physics",
        "title": "Local Clapeyron slope on a regular pure-phase coexistence branch",
        "reference": "items/pthm-td-clapeyron-local.md",
        "design_state": "Step 1 complete draft; readiness recorded separately.",
        "dependency_level": 10,
        "deps": [
          "def-td-phase-and-coexistence-domain",
          "def-td-si-quantities",
          "def-td-legendre-potentials",
          "pthm-td-intensive-coexistence-conditions",
          "pthm-td-potential-differentials",
          "pthm-td-euler-and-gibbs-duhem",
          "thm-tdmath-local-implicit-rank",
          "thm-chain-rule-for-total-derivatives",
          "def-td-reversible-process",
          "post-td-macroscopic-second-law",
          "post-td-bulk-additivity"
        ],
        "dependency_roles": {
          "def-td-phase-and-coexistence-domain": "formulation-prerequisite",
          "def-td-si-quantities": "formulation-prerequisite",
          "def-td-legendre-potentials": "formulation-prerequisite",
          "pthm-td-intensive-coexistence-conditions": "physical-result",
          "pthm-td-potential-differentials": "physical-result",
          "pthm-td-euler-and-gibbs-duhem": "physical-result",
          "thm-tdmath-local-implicit-rank": "mathematical-premise",
          "thm-chain-rule-for-total-derivatives": "mathematical-premise",
          "def-td-reversible-process": "formulation-prerequisite",
          "post-td-macroscopic-second-law": "physical-assumption",
          "post-td-bulk-additivity": "physical-assumption"
        },
        "physical_scope": "A one-component, positive-temperature, C1 coexistence branch with bilateral energy, volume, and species exchange, nonzero molar-volume jump, and the explicit local same-tag homogeneity and reversible-heat assumptions stated here, with homogeneity either independently stipulated or supplied on each designated common-law bulk branch through the local Euler theorem; no formula is asserted at critical points or nonsmooth boundaries.",
        "inventory_expansion_required": false,
        "statement": "Let $\\alpha,\\beta$ be two one-component phase branches from [[def-td-phase-and-coexistence-domain]] on a common open chart $O\\subset(0,\\infty)\\times\\mathbb R$ with coordinates $(T,p)$. Assume each branch has a local $C^2$ energy representation $\\mathcal U_i(s,V,n)$, $i\\in\\{\\alpha,\\beta\\}$, and that within each fixed branch tag it satisfies the same-tag homogeneity\n$$\n\\mathcal U_i(\\lambda s,\\lambda V,\\lambda n)=\\lambda\\mathcal U_i(s,V,n)\n$$\nfor all $\\lambda$ in a neighborhood of $1$ for which the scaled state remains in the chart. This is a phase-branch hypothesis: the general tagged law of [[post-td-bulk-additivity]] does not imply it. It may be stipulated independently on each local branch, or supplied by the common-law bulk subclass of [[pthm-td-euler-and-gibbs-duhem]] when each phase's local inverse states lie in its designated entropy cone with fixed species and intensive parameters and common SI units and energy/entropy reference conventions. That supplied subclass uses local inverse uniqueness and does not require a global energy inverse.\n\nSuppose a state $(T_0,p_0)\\in O$ is an attained interior coexistence equilibrium with bilateral energy, volume, and species exchange between the two branches, and both branches admit the valid local Gibbs charts of [[def-td-legendre-potentials]]. Write $g_i=G_i/n_i$, $s_i=S_i/n_i$, and $v_i=V_i/n_i$ in the units specified by [[def-td-si-quantities]]. If\n$$\n\\Delta v(T_0,p_0):=v_\\beta(T_0,p_0)-v_\\alpha(T_0,p_0)\\ne0,\n$$\nthen, on some open interval about $T_0$, the equal-Gibbs-per-mole coexistence condition $g_\\alpha(T,p(T))=g_\\beta(T,p(T))$ defines a unique local $C^1$ curve and\n$$\n\\frac{dp}{dT}=\\frac{s_\\beta-s_\\alpha}{v_\\beta-v_\\alpha}.\n$$\nIf, in addition, conversion from $\\alpha$ to $\\beta$ is admitted as a reversible process in contact with an ideal thermal reservoir at the same fixed $T$, then its molar latent heat absorbed by the system is $\\ell_{\\alpha\\to\\beta}=T(s_\\beta-s_\\alpha)$. These are conditional model deductions. The slope conclusion is not asserted when $\\Delta v=0$ or where the branch charts are not $C^1$.",
        "provenance": {
          "statement": "ai-altered",
          "proof": "ai-altered"
        },
        "sources": {
          "references": [
            {
              "title": "David Tong, Statistical Physics, author-hosted complete lecture notes, §§4.3.3–4.4 and 5.1.1–5.1.2",
              "url": "https://davidtong.org/teaching/statistical-physics/statmechhtml/S4"
            },
            {
              "title": "David Tong, Statistical Physics, author-hosted complete lecture notes, Chapter 5, §§5.1.1–5.1.3",
              "url": "https://davidtong.org/teaching/statistical-physics/statmechhtml/S5"
            },
            {
              "title": "Konstantin K. Likharev, Essential Graduate Physics: Statistical Mechanics, §4.1 First-order phase transitions",
              "url": "https://phys.libretexts.org/Bookshelves/Thermodynamics_and_Statistical_Mechanics/Essential_Graduate_Physics_-_Statistical_Mechanics_%28Likharev%29/04%3A_Phase_Transitions/4.01%3A_First_order_phase_transitions"
            }
          ]
        },
        "library": "physics",
        "strategy": "direct"
      },
      {
        "id": "pthm-td-compact-continuous-phase-mixture",
        "kind": "physics-theorem",
        "domain": "physics",
        "title": "Attained entropy-maximizing mixtures on compact phase domains",
        "reference": "items/pthm-td-compact-continuous-phase-mixture.md",
        "design_state": "Step 1 complete draft; readiness recorded separately.",
        "dependency_level": 9,
        "deps": [
          "def-td-phase-and-coexistence-domain",
          "post-td-concave-fundamental-entropy",
          "def-borel-sigma-algebra",
          "def-probability-measure",
          "def-tdmath-measure-integral",
          "thm-extreme-value-metric",
          "thm-tdmath-compact-continuous-mixture-attainment"
        ],
        "justified_by": [],
        "forward_refs": [],
        "dependency_roles": {
          "def-td-phase-and-coexistence-domain": "formulation-prerequisite",
          "post-td-concave-fundamental-entropy": "physical-assumption",
          "def-borel-sigma-algebra": "mathematical-premise",
          "def-probability-measure": "mathematical-premise",
          "def-tdmath-measure-integral": "mathematical-premise",
          "thm-extreme-value-metric": "mathematical-premise",
          "thm-tdmath-compact-continuous-mixture-attainment": "mathematical-premise"
        },
        "physical_scope": "Mixtures of a compact continuum of declared phase-generator states with continuous entropy and a fixed barycenter; no attainment claim is made for noncompact domains or for a different physical normalization.",
        "inventory_expansion_required": false,
        "statement": "Let $d\\ge1$, and let $K\\subseteq\\mathbb R^d$ be a nonempty compact set of dimensionless phase-generator coordinates. A generator point $x\\in K$ encodes one model-specified homogeneous phase state, with declared entropy per mole $s(x)$ in $\\mathrm{J\\,mol^{-1}K^{-1}}$; let $s:K\\to\\mathbb R$ be continuous. Define $\\operatorname{conv}K$ as the set of finite convex combinations of points of $K$, and fix $\\bar x\\in\\operatorname{conv}K$. Use the Borel sigma algebra relative to $K$, and let $\\delta_x$ denote unit point mass at $x$. The vector integral $\\int_Kx\\,dP$ is taken coordinatewise. Assume every Borel probability mixture $P$ on $K$ with $\\int_Kx\\,dP(x)=\\bar x$ is feasible and has entropy per mole $\\int_Ks(x)\\,dP(x)$. Then the entropy maximum over all such mixtures is attained by a finite atomic mixture with at most $d+1$ phase-generator states.",
        "provenance": {
          "statement": "ai-altered",
          "proof": "ai-altered"
        },
        "sources": {
          "references": [
            {
              "title": "David Tong, Statistical Physics, author-hosted complete lecture notes, §5.1.1",
              "url": "https://davidtong.org/teaching/statistical-physics/statmechhtml/S5"
            },
            {
              "title": "Konstantin K. Likharev, Essential Graduate Physics: Statistical Mechanics, §4.1 First-order phase transitions",
              "url": "https://phys.libretexts.org/Bookshelves/Thermodynamics_and_Statistical_Mechanics/Essential_Graduate_Physics_-_Statistical_Mechanics_%28Likharev%29/04%3A_Phase_Transitions/4.01%3A_First_order_phase_transitions"
            }
          ]
        },
        "library": "physics",
        "strategy": "direct"
      },
      {
        "id": "pthm-td-regular-gibbs-phase-rule",
        "kind": "physics-theorem",
        "domain": "physics",
        "title": "Local regular dimension of a reacting Gibbs phase-coexistence manifold",
        "reference": "items/pthm-td-regular-gibbs-phase-rule.md",
        "design_state": "Step 1 complete draft; readiness recorded separately.",
        "dependency_level": 10,
        "deps": [
          "def-td-phase-and-coexistence-domain",
          "def-td-equilibrium-state-domain",
          "def-td-temperature-pressure-chemical-potential",
          "pthm-td-intensive-coexistence-conditions",
          "post-td-bulk-additivity",
          "post-td-entropy-maximum",
