        "physical_scope": "A constructed two-species, one-reaction fixed-temperature and fixed-pressure model with a smooth Gibbs-potential extension to a zero-amount boundary; no empirical reaction data are claimed.",
        "inventory_expansion_required": false,
        "statement": "Use species $A,B$, one reaction column $\\nu=(-1,1)^{\\mathsf T}$, and starting amounts $n_A^0=0$ mol, $n_B^0=1$ mol. The admissible extents are $\\xi\\in[-1,0]$ mol because $n_A(\\xi)=-\\xi$ and $n_B(\\xi)=1\\,\\mathrm{mol}+\\xi$ must both be nonnegative. At fixed $T_0,p_0$, take the smooth extended constrained potential\n\\[\n\\Phi(\\xi)=\\Phi_0-(1\\,\\mathrm{J\\,mol^{-1}})\\xi .\n\\]\nAt $\\xi_*=0$ mol, let the boundary chemical potentials be $\\mu_A=0$ and $\\mu_B=-1\\,\\mathrm{J\\,mol^{-1}}$. No positive-mole thermodynamic chart at $n_A=0$ is asserted; these are the explicitly extended local model data.",
